# Two landed capabilities that had never been crossed: multi-session switching
# (rung 6) and windows-as-pane-hosts (rung 7). A switch tears down ports and
# hands the recycle bin its Release/Reopen handshake while a LENS holds retained
# pane runners over the outgoing graph.
#
# The contract this pins down, which the code chose but nothing asserted: a
# window arrangement BELONGS TO ITS SESSION, like a workspace. Switching does
# not carry your lens across; it closes the outgoing session's windows and
# reopens the incoming session's own (App::adopt_session loads that session's
# lens spaces and reopens each through the ordinary OpenWindow effect). So the
# real question is whether the whole arrangement ROUND-TRIPS, and the bin with
# it. Offline (mere://); FRESH profile.
settle 30
key escape

open mere://alpha
open mere://beta
wait
assert nodes >= 2
assert sessions == 1

# This session's recycle bin gets a record, shown in a Trail pane in the
# PRIMARY window (summon-beside follows the active pane, so the Trail must be
# established before anything moves to a lens).
act Delete node
wait
assert event node-removed
act Open Trail pane
settle 10
assert pane trail
assert row Recover mere://beta

# Now a Roster torn out to a lens: a second window holds a live runner, while
# the Trail stays behind in the primary.
act Open Roster pane
settle 5
act Tear out pane
settle 30
assert windows == 2
assert lens-pane 0:roster
assert pane trail
capture-lens 01_lens_on_first_session

# THE CROSSING: mint a new session while the lens is open. The new session has
# no arrangement of its own, so its window count is 1 — the outgoing lens is
# closed, NOT carried across — and its pane tree is its own.
act New session
wait
assert sessions == 2
assert event session-switched
assert nodes == 0
assert windows == 1
assert no-pane trail

# The bin came with us too: this session's bin is its own, so the first
# session's deleted node is not offered for recovery here.
act Open Trail pane
settle 10
assert pane trail
assert no-row Recover mere://beta
capture 02_new_session_own_bin_and_windows

# Switch BACK through the switcher lane. This is the assertion that matters:
# the first session's whole arrangement returns — the lens window reopens with
# its torn-out roster, the primary's Trail is back — and so is its bin.
omnibar actions
type switch to session
settle 5
assert suggestions >= 1
key enter
wait
settle 30
assert event session-switched
assert nodes >= 2

# The arrangement round-tripped, in both windows.
assert windows == 2
assert lens-pane 0:roster
assert pane trail
capture-lens 03_lens_restored_on_switch_back

# ...and so did the bin: the deleted node is recoverable again, here.
assert row Recover mere://beta
capture 04_bin_restored_with_its_session

log rung 7 x rung 6 (arrangement and bin both ride the session) complete
